<p>Guh. Ugh.</p>
<p>I am of <em>so</em> many minds about this.</p>
<p>It gives far more of an ending to the Hello World series, which is good. However, it doesn't feel like a &quot;real&quot; article, which is bad. It mostly feels like an extended lolFoundation joke with some creepy shit at the end, and I'm not sure it can be fully understood without first having read the original &quot;Hatbot v Mann&quot; tale <em>and</em> Hello World. Which is <em>really</em> bad.</p>
<p>That said</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&gt;hatbot: because i know everything</p>
<p>&gt;hatbot: ;P</p>
<p>&gt;hatbot: and thats just</p>
<p>&gt;hatbot: so goddamn inconvenient</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This was really good. But having read Hello World, I don't feel like this does anything but summarize what I've already read while providing that more-concrete-if-still-open ending. So I'm not going to downvote this, but as it stands, I don't think it's an article that works on its own merits. :(</p>

